{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793012867,"nonce":"MV4iizQslssYfFGLUR1o7KDcwPE=","message":"Landed in b2c7c6d52e967f348ae99378de852c8879c65de6.\n\nBrowser Terminal now uses session-owned PTYs and a bounded local screen mirror. The native engine is reused without HashLink FFI on the session side. Shell profiles come from the host, events cross the browser agent, screen patches coalesce behind acknowledgements, hidden views stop streaming, and resize requests deduplicate. Remote resize completion updates the screen only on its new revision: treating an outstanding resize as an immediate repaint had otherwise kept the LayoutTree flush loop active and delayed RPC handling. Added a delayed-screen layout regression.\n\nValidation: 11 session unit, 17 existing integration and 4 terminal integration tests pass; 7 native terminal tests and native VM primitive smoke pass. RemoteTerminalChecks with rayde_page covers late-open cancellation, Unicode/combining selection, ANSI, dirty rows, delayed resize layout and failure cleanup. Browser client tests: 23 passed. Final real-browser tests pass PTY command output/colors, resize/coalescing, hide/reopen without a new process, multiple terminals, disconnect, and no-exec availability without app failure. Full browser syntax/live-edit regression passes. Core-only and Cloudflare crate checks pass.\n\nRebuilt WASM, native terminal library and session; staged the exact tested bundle at bin/web/rayde and restarted localhost:7070 preserving URL/token/state. Live handshake, workspace read, PTY output and RAYZOR_STD_PATH smoke passed. The browser bundle loads ash_channel/blinc_abi/xgpu/xwindow without cterm. No deployment/push. Broader MSB provider/PTY execution isolation remains in 670bd15d5f2a4c8fdd82da62e9b72599f9a689affc5682a7b621f81fd72156c0.","files":null}]}